#. y1:english="Looks like you haven't||made full use of your skills.\nSome things you may not be aware of are||as follows... maybe.\nIs there anything else you want to know?\nTell me about shifting.\nIf you move by the {CU:ffff00}left analog stick{CU:ffffff} while||holding the {CU:ffff00}R1{CU:ffffff} button, you can \"shift\".\nOne drawback is that you can't run,\nbut you can move toward any direction||while always facing the enemy.\nIt's quite useful during a one on one fight||or when you want to make\nconcentrated attacks on an enemy.||Give it a try.\nTell me about guarding.\nGuard by pressing the{CU:ffff00} L1{CU:ffffff} button.\nWhen you're fighting an unarmed enemy,||as long as you make sure you don't get hit\nfrom behind, you can block||the enemy's attack almost perfectly.\nHowever, if the enemy's armed, stay alert.||A blow from a weapon will break your guard.\nAlso, guarding is useless against||knives or guns, obviously.\nTell me about dodging.\nYou can dodge by pressing {IC:00_03}➿ while shifting.\nBy using this technique, you can avoid||the enemy's attack or position yourself\nbehind the enemy.\nBy improving your \"TAI\" skills,||you will be able to move faster.\nWho the hell are you?\nMy name's Oki. I'm an apprentice of a grand||master of martial arts, Sotaro Komaki.\nI see... {PA:10}If you want to know||something, feel free to ask me.\nI'll give this to you just in case.{MS:1}{MS:0}{PA:20}||Take a look at it sometime.\nYou received \"{CC:ffc8c8}Tips from Komaki's Apprentice{CR:00}\".\n"
